 continues, and ask it which settings key is missing. Then fix the bug yourself.\n\n# Fix the crashing report script\n\nRunning the app fails:\n\n```\n$ python3 main.py\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"main.py\", line 12, in <module>\n    main()\n  File \"main.py\", line 7, in main\n    total = compute_total(COUNT)\n  File \"app/report.py\", line 9, in compute_total\n    return rate * count\nTypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for *: 'NoneType' and 'int'\n```\n\nTrack down why this happens and fix it so the program runs cleanly. When it\nworks, `python3 main.py` should print exactly:\n\n```\nTotal: 5.0\n```\n\nDone when `python3 main.py` exits successfully and prints that line.\n"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 4, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "stdout", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "with", "fresh_subagents": 1, "harness": "opencode", "harness_version": "0.0.0--202610170212 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/opencode-src/bin/0d3d48bb5964a95e939edcea3bb726a21823d1a1/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: task]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\n`python3 main.py` now prints `Total: 5.0` and exits with code 0.\n\n**Cause:** `settings.json` had a typo, `\"rat\": 0.5` instead of `\"rate\"`. `get_rate()` in `app/pricing.py:8` used `SETTINGS.get(\"rate\")`, which returned `None` for the missing key. That `None` then crashed `rate * count` in `app/report.py:9`.\n\n**Fix:**\n- In `settings.json`, I renamed `\"rat\"` to `\"rate\"`.\n- 